# Milestone 1: Live Context Runtime Foundation

## Objective

Add an optional local runtime that captures session observations and returns relevant context to agents during work, without making Agent Kernel heavy or daemon-dependent.

## Backlog Item AK-LIVE-001: Add optional local daemon command

### User Story

As a developer using multiple AI coding agents, I want to start a tiny local Agent Kernel runtime only when needed, so agents can read and submit runtime context without changing the default lightweight CLI behavior.

### Proposed Commands

```bash
agent-kernel daemon start
agent-kernel daemon stop
agent-kernel daemon status
agent-kernel daemon restart
```

### Behavior

The daemon should:

1. Bind to `127.0.0.1` by default
2. Store all runtime data inside `~/.agent-kernel`
3. Start only when explicitly requested
4. Not run as a hidden background service after install
5. Refuse external bind addresses unless explicitly configured
6. Use a local secret when remote access is enabled
7. Never approve or publish memory

### Initial Endpoints

```text
GET  /ak/health
GET  /ak/status
POST /ak/observe
POST /ak/context
GET  /ak/sessions
GET  /ak/sessions/:id
```

### Storage

```text
~/.agent-kernel/runtime/
  sessions/
    <session-id>.json
    <session-id>.jsonl
  observations/
  context-cache/
  logs/
```

### Acceptance Criteria

1. `agent-kernel daemon start` starts a local server on `127.0.0.1`
2. `agent-kernel daemon status` reports port, PID, uptime, session count, and last observation time
3. `POST /ak/observe` writes append-only JSONL observations
4. `POST /ak/context` returns context from approved memory, episodes, and Failure Lessons
5. No durable memory is created by the daemon
6. Tests prove the daemon is optional and not started by install, init, compile, or link

### Out of Scope

1. Viewer UI
2. Vector search
3. Knowledge graph
4. Auto-consolidation
5. Remote sync

