# Milestone 2: Session Capture and Timeline

## Objective

Capture what agents did during a coding session in a compact, local, replayable format that supports debugging and Failure Lessons.

## Backlog Item AK-SESSION-001: Add session model

### User Story

As a user, I want Agent Kernel to track each agent session, so I can understand what happened before a bug, edit, failure, or commit.

### Session Fields

```json
{
  "id": "session_...",
  "projectId": "agent-kernel",
  "cwd": "/path/to/repo",
  "agentId": "claude-code",
  "agentRole": "coding-agent",
  "trustLevel": "propose-only",
  "startedAt": "ISO timestamp",
  "endedAt": "ISO timestamp",
  "status": "active|completed|failed",
  "observationCount": 0,
  "linkedCommits": [],
  "linkedFailures": [],
  "summary": ""
}
```

### Commands

```bash
agent-kernel session start --agent claude-code --project .
agent-kernel session end <session-id>
agent-kernel session list
agent-kernel session show <session-id>
```

### Acceptance Criteria

1. Sessions are stored locally as JSON
2. Observations are stored as append-only JSONL
3. Session metadata references linked failures, episodes, and commits
4. Session commands do not require daemon mode if used manually
5. Unknown agents are accepted with custom `agentId`

